      "id": "msg_mockP03",
      "sessionId": "ses_mockPanelPhones",
      "seq": 3,
      "author": {
        "type": "character",
        "characterId": "chr_seedVictor"
      },
      "content": "Three points, and I shall keep them tight. First, define your terms: a ban is not guidance, not a norm, not a bell rung at the classroom door; it is state coercion applied to every pupil, and coercion demands a burden of proof its proponents have not carried. Second, a school is not a sovereign: it may regulate conduct within its gates, but a blanket prohibition substitutes a rule for the harder work of teaching judgment, and judgment is the thing phones actually require. Third, and decisively, the motion forbids the tool rather than the distraction. If a device disrupts a lesson, the school may already confiscate it; if it does not, the ban punishes the innocent to inconvenience the guilty. Define your terms, Kai, and the ban collapses under its own breadth.",
      "status": "complete",
      "createdAt": "2026-09-24T11:00:05.311Z",
