        "type": "character",
        "characterId": "chr_seedMei"
      },
      "content": "What's still open is the thing neither of my colleagues has answered: what a ban actually costs, and who pays. Amara gets a cleaner classroom; Victor gets a narrower rule. Both are real, and both are modest. My position is the stronger one because it survives the comparison — targeted restriction captures most of the attention gain without confiscating the lifeline, and it doesn't pretend a rule substitutes for teaching judgment. If you want one number, you're being sold something. The honest range still favours regulation.",
