      "author": {
        "type": "character",
        "characterId": "chr_seedVictor"
      },
      "content": "Two things remain open, and neither rescues the ban. First, the enforcement question Amara concedes she owes us: she says \"bounded hours, clear rule, exceptions built in\" — but exceptions are precisely where the discretion she condemns in Mei's proposal lives, now laundered through a nurse's note and an office stamp. Second, and decisive, nobody has met the definitional burden I set in opening: a ban is prohibition, and no one has shown the school's ordinary authority to confiscate a distracting device is insufficient. Strip the rhetoric and you have a narrower, cheaper rule that achieves the same classroom.",
